WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Your app needs an address for a name before it connects.

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.000
The client sends the question to its configured DNS resolver.

3
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.000
The resolver may already have a usable answer in its cache.

4
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.000
If needed, it asks other DNS servers to find the answer.

5
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.000
If found, the resolver replies with the requested address.

6
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Use nslookup to query a name and inspect the DNS response. Example command: nslookup app.example.com.

7
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Name resolution failure is not proof the app server is broken.
